# To create or update a token visit https://envio.dev/app/api-tokens
ENVIO_API_TOKEN="<YOUR-API-TOKEN>"

# RPC URLs, used by two effects: `getTransactionReceipt` (one
# eth_getTransactionReceipt per NFTX transaction, at most 5/s) and
# `getTokenMetadata` (name/symbol/decimals via viem multicall, once per new
# token). Event ingestion itself goes through HyperSync, including Arc;
# ApeChain still syncs over RPC (see below). Set these to override the public
# drpc.org defaults in src/utils/tokenMetadata.ts.
#
# One slot per chain in config.yaml. `getRpcUrl` still carries cases for chains
# this fork no longer indexes; they are unreachable and deliberately not listed.
ENVIO_MAINNET_RPC_URL=""
ENVIO_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=""
ENVIO_ROBINHOOD_RPC_URL=""
ENVIO_INK_RPC_URL=""
ENVIO_ARBITRUM_RPC_URL=""
# Arc receipts and token metadata still need ordinary RPC. Keep this override
# for those effects; HyperSync handles event ingestion, with no RPC fallback.
# After deploying the HyperSync config, ENVIO_RPC_URL_5042 can be removed.
# If it was your only Arc RPC override, move its value here to keep using that
# provider for effects. Otherwise effects fall back to Arc's public node.
# The old variable remains accepted as a legacy effects override until removed.
ENVIO_ARC_RPC_URL=""
# ApeChain (33139) also syncs over RPC (no HyperSync): ENVIO_RPC_URL_33139 is the
# sync endpoint in config.yaml, ENVIO_APECHAIN_RPC_URL the fallback and the
# metadata/slot0 RPC. Keep them off the shared rpc.flayer.io gateway.
ENVIO_RPC_URL_33139=""
ENVIO_APECHAIN_RPC_URL=""
